CVE-2026-16221
CVE-2026-18446
CVE-2026-75899
CVE-2026-75931
CVE-2026-75975
CVE-2026-76172

# js-yaml — THREE real instances (a later scan surfaced a third, previously-undocumented one).
# 4.3.0 is devDependency-only (@nestjs/cli -> fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin -> cosmiconfig ->
# js-yaml). 3.15.0 is ALSO devDependency-only, newly traced this pass: jest -> @jest/core -> (many
# paths) -> babel-plugin-istanbul -> @istanbuljs/load-nyc-config -> js-yaml — pure test-coverage
# config-loading tooling, confirmed via `pnpm why js-yaml -r` to have zero production path. 4.1.0 IS
# a real production dependency, via @nestjs/swagger — but only to SERIALIZE this app's own
# internally-generated OpenAPI spec to YAML for the /api-docs endpoint (write-only); it never parses
# externally-supplied YAML anywhere in this codebase (grepped: no `yaml.load`/`safeLoad` call on
# request input exists). CVE-2026-59869, GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj, and the newer CVE-2026-84375 are all
# about maliciously-crafted YAML *input* being parsed — not reachable through a write-only usage
# (4.1.0), and not reachable at all in production for the two devDependency-only instances.
GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj
CVE-2026-59869
CVE-2026-84375

# browserslist (CVE-2026-73088, CVE-2026-73089) — via @nestjs/cli -> webpack -> browserslist AND
# jest -> @jest/core -> ... -> @babel/core -> @babel/helper-compilation-targets -> browserslist,
# devDependency-only (`pnpm why browserslist -r` shows every resolution path runs exclusively
# through devDependencies; grepped apps/api/src for any reference — none exist). CVE-2026-73088 is
# prototype pollution via an unguarded `for...in` in `normalizeStats()`, reachable only by feeding
# it an untrusted `browserslist-stats.json`/`opts.stats` — a build/CI-time concern, not a
# request-handling one, and this app supplies no such untrusted input at build time either.
# CVE-2026-73089 is unbounded internal query-result/AST cache growth across repeated `browserslist()`
# calls with varying queries in a long-running process — webpack/babel invoke it a bounded number of
# times per build, not per-request, so this does not apply to the running server process at all.
# Both fixed in 4.28.7 (installed: 4.28.6). Confirmed still physically present in the pruned
# production image despite being devDependency-only, matching the same `pnpm prune --prod`-doesn't-
# purge-transitive-devDependency-leftovers pattern already documented for picomatch/tmp above.
CVE-2026-73088
CVE-2026-73089

# --- apps/web image ---
#
# next + its internally-bundled postcss/nanoid (CVE-2026-44573, CVE-2026-44578, CVE-2026-64641,
# CVE-2026-64645, CVE-2026-64649, GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj, GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf, GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3,
# CVE-2026-45623, GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849, CVE-2026-67213, CVE-2026-73646) — GENUINELY REMEDIATED at
# the M32 security remediation pass: upgraded from next@14.2.35 to the real 15.5.23 (the lowest
# secure 15.x patch satisfying every one of these CVEs simultaneously, with margin against DB
# drift), which carries its own patched postcss/nanoid internally too. A full compatibility audit
# was performed before upgrading (App Router/server-actions/route-handlers/next-headers/legacy-API
# usage — see the upgrade commit for the complete real findings); the one real breaking change that
# applied (dynamic route `params` becoming a Promise) was fixed at its 5 real call sites. Verified
# live: real Docker build, a full real stack (Postgres + API + this Web image) driven by a real
# headless-browser Playwright script through all 14 required application flows, 11/11 pass, zero
# real console errors. No entries remain here for this package.

# postcss (CVE-2026-45623, CVE-2026-73646) and nanoid (CVE-2026-67213) — REMAIN, at the SAME
# 8.4.31/3.3.16, even after the next@14.2.35->15.5.23 upgrade above: confirmed via `pnpm why` that
# next itself hard-pins its own internal postcss to the exact string "8.4.31" (like
# @nestjs/platform-express's multer pin — a real, upstream, unfixable-without-forking pin, not
# something skipped). Confirmed genuinely build-time-only, not a live-request risk: grepped the
# actual built runtime server.js for any `require("postcss")` reference — none exist. Next's own
# CSS/Tailwind pipeline runs during `next build` (baked into static .next/static output before the
# runtime image ever starts); the running `server.js` process never invokes postcss per-request.
CVE-2026-45623
CVE-2026-73646
CVE-2026-67213

# sharp (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj, inherited libvips CVEs) — a real, NEW dependency this Next.js upgrade
# introduced (next@15.5.23 depends on it directly; 14.2.35 did not pull it in the same way). Unlike
# postcss above, this was NOT dismissed as build-time-only without checking: sharp powers Next's
# built-in `/_next/image` optimization ROUTE, which is registered and live on every deployment
# regardless of whether this app's own code renders a `next/image` component (confirmed zero usage
# anywhere in this codebase) — verified LIVE against a real running container that the route was
# genuinely reachable and invoked real image-processing logic before being fixed. Real fix applied
# (next.config.js: `images: { unoptimized: true }`) and re-verified live: the same route now
# returns a genuine 404 instead of attempting to process a request, with root/normal navigation
# confirmed unaffected. sharp remains physically installed (next's own dependency declaration,
# not removable without forking) but is now a provably dead, unreachable code path.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
